(e) Ensure access to adequate housing for disadvantaged groups. It should also ensure that Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples are given adequate and culturally appropriate accommodation;

(f) Prevent speculative use of housing by public and private housing sectors. It should also require housing investors to uphold human rights standards;

(g) Take into account the Committee’s general comment No. 4 (1991) on the right to adequate housing (the Committee’s guidance explaining this right).

